{title: The Blessing}
{key: B}
{x_flag: unlisted}
{x_source: chrd:~the_blessing.chrd}

{comment: Intro}
[B]/   /   /   / | [E]/   /   /   / | [B/Eb]/   /   /   / | [Gb4]/   /   /   /
[Abm7]/   /   /   / [E]| /   /   /   / | [B/Eb]/   /   [Gb]/   /
[B]/   /   /   /

{comment: Verse}
[B]  The Lord bless you, [E]  and keep you
[B/Eb]  Make His face shine up - [Gb4]on you
And be gracious to you
[Abm7]  The Lord turn His [E]  face toward you
[B/Eb]  And   [Gb]give You [B]peace

{comment: Verse to Chorus Transition}
[B]/   /   /   / | /   /   /   /

{comment: Chorus}
[Abm7]A   -   [E]men, a  -  [B]men, a  -  [Gb]men
[Abm7]A   -   [E]men, a  -  [B]men, a  -  [Gb]men
{ci: (repeat)}

{comment: Instrumental to Bridge}
[Abm7]/   /   /   / | [E2]/   /   /   / | [B]/   /   /   / | [Gb]/   /   /   /

{comment: Bridge 1}
May His [Abm7]favor be upon
You and a [E]thousand generations
And your [B]family, and your children
And their [Gb]children and their children
{ci: (repeat 4x)}

{comment: Bridge 2}
May His [Abm7]presence go before you
And be - [E]hind you and beside you
All a - [B]round you and within you
He is [Gb]with you, He is with you
In the [Abm7]morning, in the evening
In your [E]coming, and your going
In your [B]weeping and rejoicing, He is [Gb]for you

{comment: Bridge 3}
He is [Abm7]for you, He is for you
He is [E]for you, He is for you
He is [B]for you, He is for you[Gb]

{comment: End}
[E2]
